<title>GERMANY: Veba unit says chairman in investigative custody.</title>
<headline>Veba unit says chairman in investigative custody.</headline>
<dateline>DUESSELDORF, Germany 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Veba Immobilien AG said on Friday its chairman Ulrich Lilienthal was in investigative custody, the company said.</p>
<p>Prosecutors suspect Lilienthal of using company funds to pay for private construction contracts, Veba said.  </p>
<p>The company said its supervisory board will take up the matter on Monday, and make the necessary decisions on personnel matters.</p>
<p>The investigation was first announced on Wednesday, but Lilienthal's alleged involvement was not mentioned.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
